# AI working state

Globally-useful state only. Detail lives in `state/<track>.md` — see the
index below. Read this file first every session; read a track's state file
only when you are touching that track.

## Latest

`internal/broadcast`: the fan-out primitive, with `MapChan` (map behind an
RWMutex, buffered channel per subscriber) as the reference implementation
and a benchmark harness built to compare alternatives against it. Zero
allocations on the broadcast path; the headline finding is that ~two
thirds of a broadcast's cost is waking receiver goroutines, not walking
the member set. Full detail, baseline numbers and the harness traps are in
`state/broadcast.md`. Nothing consumes the package yet — the next
milestone is still the walking skeleton (config + HTTP server + `/ws`
upgrade + read/write pumps + an `httptest`-based client test).

## State file index

- `state/broadcast.md` — `internal/broadcast`, the fan-out primitive and
  its comparative benchmark harness.

